    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This makes about 20 fritters serving 4-6 and takes about 40 minutes plus 1 hour resting. The thing to watch is the oil: use a deep thermometer or test with a small piece of batter. The fritters need oil at 175C to puff up and cook through without absorbing too much fat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Rest the batter for at least 1 hour before frying. The rest relaxes the gluten and allows the baking powder to activate, giving you puffier, lighter fritters than batter fried immediately after mixing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
